"Open Jam @ Red Stick Social","A weekly stage-time jam night welcoming solo acts and full bands alike with house drums mics and amps provided. Sign up ahead by email for a spot in the rotation.","8:00 PM","Red Stick Social","1503 Government St, Baton Rouge, LA 70802","Thursdays","","5-piece acoustic drum kit, microphones, keyboard and guitar amp plugins provided","In Person from 8:00 PM","https://redsticksocial.com/events/","<h2>Red Stick Social</h2><p>Red Stick Social is a large, multi-purpose entertainment venue in Baton Rouge's Mid City area, combining a restaurant, full bar, bowling lanes and a stage under one roof. Since opening in 2019, it has positioned itself as one of the capital city's premier gathering spots for food, drinks and live entertainment.</p><h3>Atmosphere and Setting</h3><p>The space is spacious and modern, with a dedicated performance area, professional sound and lighting, and enough room to host everything from intimate acoustic nights to full-band showcases alongside its bowling and dining areas.</p><h3>Open Jam Night</h3><p>Red Stick Social hosts a weekly Thursday night Open Jam, welcoming solo performers, full bands and everyone in between to sign up for stage time. The house provides a five-piece acoustic drum kit, multiple microphones, keyboard and guitar amp plugins, and even camera stands so performers can record their sets, with a rotation of regular jam night hosts keeping the evening moving.</p><h3>Other Programming</h3><p>Beyond the weekly jam, Red Stick Social's calendar includes happy hours, themed dance nights, karaoke, watch parties for LSU and Saints games, and a weekend brunch series.</p><h3>For Performers</h3><p>Performers are asked to sign up in advance by emailing the venue's music team, after which they are placed on the evening's stage-time rotation.</p><h3>Good to Know</h3><p>Red Stick Social is located at 1503 Government St, Baton Rouge, LA 70802, in the heart of Mid City.</p>"
